From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 02 Nov 2026 18:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: PS5: The log says where a large reservation landed.

Patch 0891 logs a reservation that failed or was refused. One of 4 GiB or more that succeeds now says where it landed
and where it was asked for. Steam's browser in the title (e1-webhelper-title-base-2026-11-02-03) had its V8 cage and
sandbox requests refused above the console's address space, and then faulted reading 0x400015F1F8 on a page that was
not there: a cage base of 0x4000000000 plus a 32-bit offset, by its shape, but no line said where V8's fallback
reservation went.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index 1026e50..8fb7619 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -7229,6 +7229,11 @@ static NTSTATUS allocate_virtual_memory( void **ret, SIZE_T *size_ptr, ULONG typ
             else if (status)
                 fprintf( stderr, "wine-ps5: reserving %#lx bytes at %p refused: %#x (type %#x, protect %#x, align %#lx)\n",
                          (unsigned long)size, base, status, type, protect, (unsigned long)align );
+            /* Where a large reservation landed (a V8 pointer cage is 4 GiB at a 4 GiB boundary): the refusals above
+             * say only where it did not. */
+            else if (size >= ((SIZE_T)4 << 30))
+                fprintf( stderr, "wine-ps5: reserved %#lx bytes at %p (asked %p, type %#x, protect %#x, align %#lx)\n",
+                         (unsigned long)size, view->base, base, type, protect, (unsigned long)align );
 #endif
 
             if (status == STATUS_SUCCESS)
